          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"lafayette-la-princesse-de-cleves-63e18c98a4bf1337\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"Monsieur de Clèves directly presents his former love for his wife as a true, exceptionally deep emotional state. The imperfect « je vous aimais » is retrospective but still plainly avowal-like and truth-conditional. In this comparative clause he does not undertake or renew a relational commitment; instead, he contrasts his past marital love with the allegedly self-interested professions of seducers. Although the larger speech is emotionally uncontrolled and delivered near death, the highlighted words function as part of a reasoned accusation and self-description rather than as a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The surrounding speech results from feelings he can no longer contain, but that narrative fact concerns the occasion and intensity of delivery; it does not provide strong independent E force for this syntactically integrated comparison.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Monsieur de Clèves speaks the retrospective love avowal directly to Madame de Clèves, embedded within the comparison « être aimée comme je vous aimais ».\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Dying and believing himself cruelly deceived, Monsieur de Clèves uses the avowal within a farewell, reproach, and moral contrast. He characterizes his own passion as true and legitimate and opposes it to men who profess love merely to gain the honor of seduction. This framing makes the utterance accusatory and self-vindicating, but those functions operate through a claim about the reality and quality of his past love rather than through a new undertaking.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"« vous connaîtrez la différence d'être aimée comme je vous aimais, à l'être par des gens qui, en vous témoignant de l'amour, ne cherchent que l'honneur de vous séduire »\",\"supports\":\"The highlighted clause asserts the distinctive reality and quality of his past love while contrasting it with instrumental professions of love; this strongly supports T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"« un homme qui vous aimait d'une passion véritable et légitime »\",\"supports\":\"The nearby explicit characterization of his passion as true and legitimate corroborates the truth-conditional avowal and its marital, self-vindicating framing.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narrator says that his conflicting and painful feelings were such « qu'il ne les put renfermer en lui-même »; the highlighted phrase nevertheless occurs later inside an extended comparative argument.\",\"supports\":\"There is strong emotional pressure behind the speech, but the highlighted utterance remains syntactically and rhetorically integrated into an assertion, so this does not independently establish E.\",\"confidence\":0.94},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"« je meurs sans regret, puisque je n'ai pu l'avoir, et que je ne puis plus le désirer »\",\"supports\":\"He frames the relationship as ending rather than undertaking or renewing a commitment, weighing against P for the highlighted retrospective avowal.\",\"confidence\":0.95}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core force as a retrospective avowal of loving feeling. The reproachful, comparative, marital, and self-vindicating dimensions belong to contextual use and do not require either E or O; no undertaking force is independently present.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"The French imperfect marks the love as viewed retrospectively; it does not weaken the utterance's status as a presentation of an emotional state as true.\"}"
        }
